            <ArticleTitle>Evaluating pressure-relieving mattresses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>177-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this study, three mattresses were evaluated to assess their effectiveness in relation to the pain and discomfort experienced by 40 patients with neurological disorders who had Waterlow scores &gt; or = 15 and required pressure support. The results indicate that one mattress (the Quattro DC2000) performed significantly better than the other two (Nimbus II and Pegasus Airwave).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
